WEBVTT

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:03.230
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:09.530
l'd really like to thank you for joining us today for this ocean tour of Saitama.

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:14.610
This ship is currently floating over
Tokyo, the old capital of Japan.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:17.330
Please look to your right.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:22.280
The islands you see there are the Bosohan lslands of what was once Chiba prefecture.

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:24.880
As you all know, 20 years ago Chiba prefecture...

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.870
...was submerged when Japan was struck by the worldwide disaster...

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:32.880
...which flooded more than 95% of the world's land area.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:37.640
Along with Tokyo, it lost its prefecture title...

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:42.410
...and the islands are all that remain of it today.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:44.770
And now please look to your left.

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:48.410
You will see a steel tower.

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:52.020
That was once the world-famous Tokyo Tower,

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:55.380
which was the first radio broadcast tower in the Pacific.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:59.370
The Tokyo Tower, which once stood at a height of 333 meters

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:01.540
still has the number one observation deck above water,

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:05.730
although now tilted at a 23.7 degree angle.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:10.580
It is now used as a marine radio navigation beacon tower.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:13.050
And now, ladies and gentlemen, if you'd look down.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:22.750
I'm sure you can see the buildings spread out underwater.

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:28.060
These are the flooded remains of Tokyo, once the capital of Japan.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.740
The lights you see below us mark the various areas...

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:35.870
...in which underwater Salvager
work vessels are in operation.

00:01:35.870 --> 00:01:39.980
Salvaging, which is work to recover precious goods and data...

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:43.620
which were lost underwater in the great catastrophe,

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:47.320
was a new profession born after the disaster occurred.

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:02.100
Everything about you is everything to me.

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:05.180
I don't want to hold back anymore!

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:10.190
I remember. We got G.D.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:12.900
Let's follow the course where our curiosity leads...

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.820
...and I know a wondrous power will be born.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:20.910
Silent City. We're Salvagers.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:23.740
Let's go out sometime and try to find...

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:26.750
...the skyscrapers in the sunken cities below.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:31.330
Don't be afraid. Come together.

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:36.670
As the sun shines down upon us...

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:42.100
...now, let's try to recover...

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:47.180
...everything that's been lost!

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:53.310
Let's journey beyond time!

00:02:53.310 --> 00:03:00.780
I miss you! I want to take it to you!

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:04.080
I don't want you to forget about me.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:09.040
I take you! Because there is...

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:15.040
...a shining world that no one's ever seen!

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.010
Let it go!

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:23.180
Forever...

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:46.090
Aika, are you okay?

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:49.610
I'm fine. Just a little further...

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:51.210
Got it!

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:58.630
Let's see... Serial number 2069107.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:01.860
It checks out as an
Atlantic lndustries data casing.

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.090
In other words...

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:05.050
Recovery, complete!

00:04:05.630 --> 00:04:08.930
Wow, l'd never guess it was 20 years old.

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:11.730
All right, let's grab a cold beer topside.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:13.820
Screw, bearing to port!

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:20.610
That...!

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:21.650
Gusto!

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:25.360
Yo!

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:27.410
That's ours! Give it back!

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:30.200
If you want it, go out with me.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:31.620
Oh, get real!

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:36.670
Hey! What the...?! Cut it out!
Give it back!

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:41.800
You've got a lot to learn about using that machine, Gusto.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:42.960
See ya!

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:44.760
Damn it, Aika! Come back!

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:47.780
Serves you right!

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:50.850
Rion!

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:52.310
Gusto!

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:54.810
It wasn't me! Look outside! Look!

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:04.110
This is turning bad! Run for it!

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:05.700
AIKA!!!

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:07.660
Emergency rise!

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:11.080
What's...?

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:37.550
All right, that's enough. Dive.

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:40.150
Yes, sir. Prepare to dive!

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:42.610
Prepare to dive!

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:57.920
It's been damaged.

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:02.380
The best I can give you is half price.

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:05.780
Oh, please! Give us a break!

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:08.480
You saw the news yesterday, didn't you?

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:12.670
Can't you give us credit for recovering it from that explosion?

00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:14.220
Even taking that into account...

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:18.460
C'mon... Pretty please?

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:19.730
No.

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:22.650
You stupid, mean, cheap, no good, son of a...

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:27.950
That's enough out of you! Go into the trailer NOW!

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:30.460
But! But! But!

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:36.970
Can't you cut it out? Honestly...

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:38.250
But, Daddy...

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:42.540
Boss. I've told you to call me that during business hours.

00:06:43.740 --> 00:06:45.080
Wait!

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:52.140
Look, we already charge less than anyone else does.

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:57.170
Are you listening? Daddy!

00:06:57.170 --> 00:06:58.020
Boss.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:00.210
Oh, like it matters!

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:05.070
Our policy is not to charge in cases like these.

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:09.020
Don't you understand that stubborn pride...

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:11.150
...is what's gotten us into this situation?

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:15.360
I've said it over and over!
We're not running a charity here!

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:17.580
What are we going to do about all these bills?

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.810
For every one we pay off, we get two more!

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:22.040
We never break even,
no matter how hard we work!

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:25.500
Rion, to be a Salvager is...

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.800
Oh, l'm sick of hearing about that!

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:33.530
You think you can still run things the old way.

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:36.690
Maybe you were the top man in the business years ago...

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:40.410
...but now nouveau riche playboys like Gusto are on top...

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:42.960
...while we're stuck in debtor's hell!

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:46.130
It's time to shut the photo album on the good old days!

00:07:46.130 --> 00:07:48.030
Face reality, would you? Reality!

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:53.070
I'm really amazed Aika works so hard for you and doesn't just quit.

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:56.940
Especially when your own daughter just wants to call it quits...

00:07:57.690 --> 00:08:01.290
I know! lf things fall apart, we can turn independent!

00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:06.610
Between her top-class skill and me helping out, there'd be nothing to fear!

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:08.990
Nothing to fear, huh?

00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:10.130
Aika!

00:08:13.730 --> 00:08:15.090
I'm back, sir.

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:17.400
Ah, thank you, Aika.

00:08:17.690 --> 00:08:19.640
Where were you, Aika?

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:23.600
We had some loan payments due today.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:31.110
Look, Aika, I have to talk to you about something.

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:36.940
K2 Corporation.

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:43.690
You again? Look, about the case...
I turned down that job, didn't l?

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:47.250
No! I don't care how many times you ask me!

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:52.300
You stubborn...!
lt's not a question of the money!

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:54.440
Uh, Aika, the truth is...

00:08:54.440 --> 00:08:56.250
I don't care how much...

00:08:56.680 --> 00:09:00.750
I'll take over here.
Sorry about the other day.

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:04.210
Yes. Yes, we'll be glad to take the job.

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:07.560
Right. Right. I understand.

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:10.750
Then we'll head over there right now.

00:09:11.290 --> 00:09:12.940
Right. Good-bye.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:15.410
Aika, what are you doing?

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:17.420
What it looks like, sir.

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:20.120
You know what kind of job it is, don't you?!

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:22.750
This is no time for pride, sir.

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:25.490
You needn't worry yourself about me.

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:26.210
Umm...

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:32.740
This is my home.
I just want to protect it.

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:37.530
Oh, right! You wanted to
discuss something with me, Rion?

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:41.220
Oh! Uh, never mind!
Nothing important.

00:10:19.120 --> 00:10:21.290
I've brought Mr. Gusto.

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:25.660
Well, if it isn't Aika. You usually
don't come to places like this.

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:28.650
Doesn't your company usually
pass on jobs like this?

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:31.260
Lagu?

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:38.220
Yes. It's a new energy source being
developed by a certain agency.

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:40.860
We'd like you to confirm the existence of Lagu...

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:44.700
...and obtain any research data they have on it.

00:10:46.600 --> 00:10:49.580
I understand.
So, what about the payment?

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:54.620
100 million if you get the data.
100 million for Lagu or a sample.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:57.450
If you get both, you get 300 million.

00:10:57.450 --> 00:10:59.300
Is that acceptable?

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:00.760
Very well, then.

00:11:07.160 --> 00:11:08.600
Who are they?

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:26.490
Can we help you?

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:32.830
Whoa! Ladies, hold on a sec...

00:11:48.750 --> 00:11:49.100
Aika!

00:12:08.570 --> 00:12:09.330
Why, you...!

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:24.240
That's enough.

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:32.190
Are you okay?
Thank goodness you're all right!

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:36.440
Telling us this was all a joke isn't gonna cut it.

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:38.400
Who are you?

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:47.740
Y- You...!

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:51.840
Sorry, but I gave your secretary a little time off!

00:12:57.820 --> 00:13:01.180
I'd heard about you Salvagers.

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:03.470
Now l've seen it.
You're pretty good.

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:07.140
You've taken very good care of my underlings.

00:13:08.210 --> 00:13:11.710
We... We're sorry, ma'am!
Please for...

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:15.060
Useless fool!

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:16.900
That's horrible!

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:23.280
If you don't pass on this job, don't be surprised if you end up like this.

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:25.740
Aika!

00:13:28.540 --> 00:13:31.890
And just what's your connection to this job?

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:34.410
There's no reason for you to know, is there?

00:13:34.890 --> 00:13:37.210
Oh, but that's not true.

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:40.380
It's vital data for our assignment, isn't it?

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:42.960
You don't want to live, do you?

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:51.930
Well, they told me not to raise
too much of a fuss in this country.

00:13:54.360 --> 00:13:56.060
Recovery, complete.

00:13:56.060 --> 00:13:59.470
All right.
This is your final warning.

00:13:59.470 --> 00:14:02.150
Stay out of this, or else!

00:15:05.850 --> 00:15:07.660
These are your instructions.

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:09.550
They said to read them once you're in the plane.

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:12.390
Okay, leave this to me.

00:15:12.560 --> 00:15:15.060
Please, Aika, we promised.

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:17.180
We swore we'd never touch these jobs again.

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:19.700
You're upset, aren't you?

00:15:20.430 --> 00:15:22.660
I haven't forgotten.

00:15:22.660 --> 00:15:27.200
Do you still blame yourself for
what forced me into retirement?

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:28.340
I've told you.

00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:29.880
I know.

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:31.480
I know...

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:32.990
Then why?

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:37.910
Because losing the company and Rion would be worse than breaking that promise.

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:41.280
Don't worry. If anything happens, l'll use this.

00:15:42.450 --> 00:15:43.360
I see.

00:15:43.360 --> 00:15:44.930
I'd better get going.

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:48.560
All right, but this is the
last time. Is that clear?

00:15:48.940 --> 00:15:50.010
I'm sorry.

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:54.640
And, Aika...

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:56.770
Don't get in over your head.

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:13.880
From here, maintain a heading of
1-5-0 and head for the shore...

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:18.560
Rion!

00:16:24.190 --> 00:16:26.420
What are you doing here?!

00:16:27.390 --> 00:16:31.380
Why do you think?
To assist you, of course!

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:35.680
We're headed back!

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:37.330
You can't!

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:38.530
Yes, I can!

00:16:38.530 --> 00:16:41.390
Today's job is different.
Anyway, l'm going back!

00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:45.450
Hold it! What do you
think you're doing, Rion?!

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:49.700
If you're so set on turning back,
l'll just jump out right here!

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:51.600
Don't try to bluff me, Rion.

00:16:51.600 --> 00:16:56.210
I'm not bluffing! I want to
assist you, no matter what!

00:16:56.880 --> 00:16:59.700
All right!
All right, just stop that!

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:00.620
I won't!

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:00.900
I want to help!

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:04.460
Aika! Still flying that junkheap?

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:09.490
I'll go on ahead and l'll let
you admire my treasure later.

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:11.790
Don't work too hard!

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:18.370
See? You gonna let him
get away with saying that?

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:20.290
Hm, Aika...?

00:17:20.570 --> 00:17:25.940
If you let him get it first, we'll have to listen to that muscle-bound jerk bragabout it for the next 10 years.

00:17:26.890 --> 00:17:29.900
Oh, I see.
Well, then, l'll just get off here.

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:31.610
Fine, do what you like.

00:17:40.600 --> 00:17:43.160
Excuse me!
Do you have a moment, Miss Nena?

00:17:46.970 --> 00:17:47.880
What is it?

00:17:48.240 --> 00:17:52.090
Yes, ma'am! That Salvager's plane
appears to be headed this way.

00:17:53.950 --> 00:17:56.050
Understood.
I'll be there in a minute.

00:17:56.650 --> 00:17:57.890
Air raid!

00:17:58.220 --> 00:17:59.250
Right!

00:18:04.530 --> 00:18:06.130
Is this all right, Miss Nena?

00:18:06.130 --> 00:18:08.280
Attacking without telling Mr. Hargen?

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:12.070
No need. We don't have to bother
my brother with these trifles!

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:13.740
Okay, Bandra.

00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:16.600
We'll reach our target point in
the island sector in a few minutes.

00:18:16.600 --> 00:18:18.320
Roger!

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:20.530
Gusto, check out that ship!

00:18:21.090 --> 00:18:22.330
Don't you think that's weird?

00:18:22.330 --> 00:18:25.970
What do you mean "weird"?
Huh?

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:29.500
Missiles!

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:30.750
Run for it, Bandra!

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:31.470
Gotcha!

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:41.180
What are you doing?!
Shoot that thing down!

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:42.420
Another plane approaching!

00:18:45.460 --> 00:18:47.140
I'm going out!
Prepare the Regulus!

00:18:48.780 --> 00:18:52.130
Hargen, just how long are
you going to make me wait?

00:18:52.600 --> 00:18:56.270
Just wait a little longer,
Captain. It's nearly ready.

00:18:56.270 --> 00:18:58.670
Are you going to prove it this time?

00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:01.120
Oh? Are you saying that l'm lying to you?

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:06.080
Now that you mention it, we appear to have a leak here.

00:19:06.080 --> 00:19:11.610
I've been getting more and more
distractions to my work lately.

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:14.340
Have you heard anything about it?

00:19:14.580 --> 00:19:17.570
No. I'll get my people to work on it.

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:19.380
Then l'll leave it to you.

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:24.010
Does he think I don't know anything?

00:19:24.330 --> 00:19:26.980
Once I have the Lagu, I won't need that stupid ape.

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:38.570
Regulus, ready to launch!

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:55.590
Here they come again!

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:58.930
One, two, three, four... Four of them!

00:20:05.050 --> 00:20:06.240
All right!

00:20:06.240 --> 00:20:07.810
Don't relax too soon!

00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:10.390
Incoming from above!

00:20:13.250 --> 00:20:15.660
It's on our tail!
Shake it off!

00:20:15.660 --> 00:20:17.250
I'm trying!

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:18.030
They've locked on!

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:23.200
Gusto!

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:29.660
You're next!

00:20:31.210 --> 00:20:35.570
Do you think you can escape
my Regulus in that antique?!

00:20:48.240 --> 00:20:50.020
The Lagu detector's reading something.

00:20:50.560 --> 00:20:52.460
All right, we're here.
Contact Nena.

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:55.490
Yes, sir. Direction: 1-3-0.
Distance: 15,000.

00:20:57.050 --> 00:21:01.610
Mr. Hargen! Miss Nena is
engaging a plane right now.

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:05.810
Damn it, Nena! What are you
doing at a time like this?!

00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:08.370
Call her back!
Tell her not to bother with it!

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:16.640
Miss Nena, return at once!
These are Mr. Hargen's orders!

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:19.860
All right! l'll come back as
soon as l've shot this one down!

00:21:19.860 --> 00:21:21.380
Miss Nena, these are Mr. Hargen's ord...

00:21:22.130 --> 00:21:24.840
How dare she challenge me in
that broken-down museum piece!

00:21:25.320 --> 00:21:27.020
Regulus refusing to return to base.

00:21:27.020 --> 00:21:28.560
Enough! That idiot...

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:32.620
Reading increasing! l've never
seen such a strong reaction!

00:21:34.820 --> 00:21:36.650
Aika, behind us! Behind us!

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:39.770
I know, but I can't do anything
about the difference in speed!

00:21:40.040 --> 00:21:42.320
No, not that! Behind THEM!

00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:51.200
There, you see?
l've caught up with you.

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:53.340
This time l'll shoot you down!

00:21:55.650 --> 00:21:58.820
What?! The brake isn't working!
But why?!

00:22:06.370 --> 00:22:08.500
Damn! Engine failure!

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:10.500
Losing oil pressure!
Engine revs dropping!

00:22:13.690 --> 00:22:15.620
Why?! What's wrong?!

00:22:15.620 --> 00:22:19.640
Electronic sys...ems don't
f..-nction in Lagu det'cti___n zone!

00:22:19.640 --> 00:22:21.090
What?! Big Brother!

00:22:21.090 --> 00:22:22.110
Eject!

00:22:24.410 --> 00:22:26.610
Send out the launch to recover Nena.

00:22:26.610 --> 00:22:28.610
She's caused us enough trouble.

00:22:29.010 --> 00:22:33.050
But, my God, this is huge!
With a reaction this big...!

00:22:36.720 --> 00:22:39.040
No good! I can't
restart the engine!

00:22:39.640 --> 00:22:41.970
Altitude: dropping! Engine revs:
zero! Hydraulics: out!

00:22:41.970 --> 00:22:44.180
Emergency hydro pump...
Everything's out!

00:22:44.180 --> 00:22:45.470
If I don't do something...

00:22:45.890 --> 00:22:47.260
Rion! Rion!

00:22:50.730 --> 00:22:51.890
I wasn't calling you.

00:22:54.860 --> 00:22:56.600
I said I wasn't calling you!

00:22:57.150 --> 00:22:58.270
Hey...

00:22:58.730 --> 00:23:00.100
Hold it!

00:23:02.900 --> 00:23:06.150
I said I could handle this situation...myself!

00:23:13.710 --> 00:23:17.250
Damn it, why do you have to be so rough?

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:19.630
No time for complaining.

00:23:20.340 --> 00:23:23.300
In this case, I have to have you do what you can do.

00:23:23.300 --> 00:23:24.100
Let's go!

00:23:35.570 --> 00:23:36.810
Okay, here goes!

00:23:37.740 --> 00:23:40.840
Before starting engine check!
Throttle: closed!

00:23:40.840 --> 00:23:42.670
Engine master switch:
check on!

00:23:43.040 --> 00:23:43.900
Okay, spin it!

00:23:52.060 --> 00:23:56.620
Engine revs: 40%. Oil pressure:
nominal. Throttle, start idle!

00:23:57.760 --> 00:24:00.050
Exhaust temperature and
fuel flow: looking good.

00:24:00.050 --> 00:24:00.970
Power!

00:24:10.880 --> 00:24:12.300
C'mon, work!

00:25:54.740 --> 00:25:58.830
Let's go out into the bustling city.

00:26:01.410 --> 00:26:09.170
I just want to slip off my boots and walk along with the wind.

00:26:10.380 --> 00:26:14.550
That feeling of honesty that I had forgotten...

00:26:16.930 --> 00:26:24.890
...is reawakened with just a single deep breath.

00:26:26.020 --> 00:26:29.980
As I sit by the window in the moonlight...

00:26:29.980 --> 00:26:34.860
...with my chin cupped in my hand...

00:26:34.860 --> 00:26:40.410
...I find myself thinking of you.

00:26:40.410 --> 00:26:49.040
Though I have kept it in my
heart for such a... such a long time...

00:26:49.040 --> 00:26:56.170
...without thinking, I look back at the person I used to be.

00:26:56.170 --> 00:27:04.100
I know, oh, I know.
It's because I'm much more naive than I look.

00:27:04.600 --> 00:27:14.570
Always wavering,
caught somewhere between cowardice and arrogance.

00:27:27.410 --> 00:27:35.920
Since those feelings are
growing stronger and stronger inside...

00:27:35.920 --> 00:27:43.100
...I gradually feel that there's a new tomorrow for me.

00:27:43.100 --> 00:27:47.520
Though I may hesitate, though I may dream...

00:27:47.520 --> 00:27:51.650
Though I may keep taking the long way around...

00:27:51.650 --> 00:27:55.570
...when I eventually reach that place...

00:27:55.570 --> 00:28:01.700
...I want to be met by your smiling face.

00:28:34.280 --> 00:28:35.880
We've been captured...

00:28:35.880 --> 00:28:39.060
...by the mysterious mad scientist, Dr. Hargen.

00:28:39.060 --> 00:28:43.290
They've stripped us of everything.
Escape is impossible.

00:28:43.290 --> 00:28:46.330
Huh? Stripped of everything?!

00:28:46.330 --> 00:28:49.470
That means they're gonna do this,
and that, and all sorts of stuff!

00:28:49.470 --> 00:28:53.250
I just can't handle this!
Aika, do something, please!

00:28:53.250 --> 00:28:54.860
No... Stop it!

00:28:55.240 --> 00:28:58.340
No! My body can't take much more of this!

00:28:58.620 --> 00:29:00.800
Aika! What's wrong?!

00:29:01.040 --> 00:29:04.380
Aika, next trial: Naked Mission.

00:29:04.700 --> 00:29:07.550
Something awakens from a naked Aika.
